<SiteLayout title="Learning That Grows With Your Child | Growing Kids" description="See how ELM, Conscious Discipline and purposeful play support learning and kindergarten readiness at Growing Kids." breadcrumbs={[{name:"Learning That Grows With Your Child",path:"/curriculum/"}]}><section class="page-hero"><div class="wrap"><h1>Learning That Grows With Your Child</h1><p class="intro">Growing Kids uses ELM (Early Learning Matters) with Conscious Discipline to support learning and kindergarten readiness. Hands-on play, caring relationships and classroom routines help children practice academic, social and physical skills.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href="/book-a-tour/">Schedule a Tour</a></div></div></section>
<section class="section sage"><div class="wrap split"><div data-care-reveal><h2>Small discoveries become everyday skills.</h2><p>ELM gives teachers a framework for purposeful learning. Children explore through stories, conversation, art, movement and hands-on activities. Teachers make room for children’s ideas as well as guided experiences.</p><p>At home, ask what your child built, which story they heard or who they played with. These simple conversations connect classroom discoveries with family life.</p><a class="text-link" href="/programs/preschool/">See preschool in practice</a></div><img src="/images/early-writing.webp" alt="A child practicing pencil control in the classroom" width="700" height="600" loading="lazy" data-shoot="replace"/></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap split"><div data-care-reveal><h2>Learning to be together.</h2><p>Conscious Discipline supports the social and emotional side of learning. Naming feelings, building relationships and practicing ways to solve problems belong alongside counting and stories.</p><p>Ask your teacher which words and routines your child is practicing so you can build on them at home.</p></div><div data-care-reveal><h2>Play has a purpose.</h2><p>On Main Street, children explore a child-size town through pretend play. They take on roles, talk with friends and try out ideas. Outdoor play gives them another place to move and discover when the weather allows.</p><a class="text-link" href="/why-choose-us/">See the Growing Kids Difference</a></div></div></section><section class="section cream"><div class="wrap"><h2>A rhythm for every age.</h2><p>Classrooms adapt activities and timing to the children. These examples describe the kinds of experiences to discuss on your tour, rather than a fixed daily timetable.</p><div class="wide-table"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Age group</th><th scope="col">Learning and play</th><th scope="col">Care and connection</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Infants</th><td>One-to-one interaction, sounds and gentle exploration</td><td>Individual feeding, sleep and care routines</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Toddlers</th><td>Stories, art, movement and first friendships</td><td>Meals, rest and practice with everyday skills</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Preschool</th><td>Language, early math, science and imaginative play</td><td>Group routines, friendships and time to rest</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">School age</th><td>Homework, group activities and indoor or outdoor play</td><td>Before and after school transitions</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="review-note"><strong>Classroom schedule coming</strong>Exact daily schedules by age group are awaiting center confirmation.</p></div></section><section class="section"><div class="wrap split"><h2>Licensed is the starting point.</h2><div><p>Indiana licensing sets the requirements a child care center must meet. NECPA accreditation and Indiana’s Paths to QUALITY Level 4 are earned quality recognitions on top of licensing.</p><p>Growing Kids identifies its centers as NECPA accredited and Level 4. Ask your director to explain what those standards mean in your child’s classroom.</p><a class="text-link" href="/locations/">Explore our centers</a><p><a href="/minds-in-motion/">Read about movement activities</a></p></div></div></section>
</SiteLayout>